+The first cancellation starts the escalation deadline; repeated SIGINT/SIGTERM
+cannot extend it or an already-running cleanup stage. A procfs entry disappearing
+between open and read is ordinary process-table churn (ENOENT or ESRCH), while
+unrelated read errors remain fatal rather than being hidden.
+
 Non-Linux platforms exec the command directly and retain their normal init
 reaping. Linux subreaper setup failure is fatal; there is no fallback claiming
 these physical-absence assertions passed. A denied operation is an error.
